  [282, "In a forest, the hunter knows that if he uses camouflage, he can get close to the deer undetected. He also knows that if he moves quietly, he can avoid startling the deer. However, moving quietly in camouflage gear is challenging. The hunter can either use camouflage or move quietly. Does this mean the hunter will either get close to the deer undetected or avoid startling the deer?", "True."],
