  [1061, "Example 1:  \n{P}: Mary studies hard for the exam.\n{Q}: Mary passes the exam.\n{R}: Mary gets stuck in traffic on the way to the exam.  \n{S}: Mary arrives late for the exam.\n{T}: Mary does not get to finish the exam. Story:", "True."],
  [1062, "Jenny likes walking to school in the mornings. If the weather report says no rain today, Jenny will walk to school. If Jenny finished her homework last night, she'll meet up with friends before class starts. Either she won't walk to school or she won't meet up with friends, or maybe she'll do neither. Jenny checks her planner to see what day it is. She knows that if today is Tuesday, then she finished her homework last night. If the weather report says no rain today, is today Tuesday?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1063, "Jenny wants to go out with friends tonight. If she finished her homework, Jenny can go to the movies. If it's Sunday night, she'll also get pizza with them. Either she won't go to the movies or she won't get pizza, or maybe she'll do neither. She checks her calendar to see what day it is. She knows that if she has school tomorrow, then it must be Sunday night. If Jenny finished her homework, does she have school tomorrow?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1064, "The actor wowed audiences with his performance in the new drama film. If the actor gave a great performance, the film will win awards. If the actor did extensive preparation for the role, he'll get offered more serious roles in the future. Either the film won't win awards or he won't get more serious roles, or maybe neither will happen. The actor remembers that this role required learning a new skill. He knows that if the role required learning a new skill, then he did extensive preparation for the role. If the actor gave a great performance, did the role require learning a new skill?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1065, "Omar's morning commute is easier when traffic is light. If traffic is light, Omar will arrive to work on time. If fewer people are commuting, Omar will also stop for an iced coffee on the way. Either he won't make it to work on time or he won't stop for coffee, or he may do neither. He considers why traffic might be light. He knows that if many people are on vacation, then fewer people are commuting. If traffic is light, are many people on vacation?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1066, "Alex needs gas in his car to drive to work and a clear schedule to meet friends for dinner. If the car has gas, Alex can drive to work. If Alex's schedule is clear after work, he'll meet friends for dinner. Either he won't drive to work or he won't meet for dinner, or maybe neither. Alex checks his calendar to see what day it is. He knows that if it's Friday, his schedule is clear after work. If the car has gas in the tank, is it Friday?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1067, "Sara wants to give her friend a nice birthday gift. If the package was delivered on time, she can wrap the gift. If her gift wrapping supplies arrived, she can add a handmade card.  Either she can't wrap the gift or she can't add a handmade card, or maybe neither. Sara checks her calendar to see the date. She knows that if it is her friend's birthday today, then her gift wrapping supplies arrived. If the package was delivered on time, is it Sara's friend's birthday today?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1068, "Lucy wants to enjoy her Friday night. If she finished her homework, she can go out with friends. If she cleaned her room, she can watch a movie tonight. She has a feeling that she can't go out with friends or she can't watch a movie, or neither today. Lucy checks her calendar and sees that if it's Friday, then she will clean her room. If Lucy finished her homework, is it Friday?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1069, "Michelle wants to make dinner and try a new dessert recipe for her family. If the recipe only requires pantry staples, Michelle can make dinner. If Michelle went grocery shopping this week, she will also try a new dessert. Either she won't make dinner or she won't make dessert, or maybe she'll do neither. She reflects on when she last went to the store. She knows that if Michelle got paid last Friday, then she went grocery shopping this week. If the recipe only requires pantry staples, did Michelle get paid last Friday?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1070, "Miriam wants to make dinner and dessert but needs to check if she has the ingredients. If the recipe only requires pantry staples, Miriam can make dinner tonight. If she went grocery shopping this week, she'll also bake cookies for dessert. Either she won't make dinner or she won't bake cookies, or she'll do neither. She checks the fridge to see if she has dairy products. She knows that if milk and eggs are there, then she went grocery shopping this week. If the recipe only requires pantry staples, are milk and eggs in the refrigerator?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1071, "Amy needs a working car to drive to her morning doctor's appointment and get coffee. If her car is working, she'll drive to the appointment. If it's in the morning, she'll get coffee on the way. Either she won't drive or won't get coffee, or neither. Amy checks the weather to see if the roads are okay. She knows that if there's no snow or ice, her appointment is in the morning. If Amy's car is working, are the roads free of snow and ice?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1072, "Jenny wants to go out with friends, but only if she finishes her homework first. If Jenny finished all her homework, she can go out. If her curfew is midnight, she can stay out late. Either she can't go out or she can't stay out late, or maybe neither. Jenny checks her planner to see what day is next. She knows that if tomorrow is Saturday, her curfew is midnight. If Jenny finished all her homework, is tomorrow Saturday?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1073, "Michelle wants to take a drive to the mountains and go shopping downtown. If the car has enough gas, she can drive to the mountains. If Michelle got her paycheck this week, she'll also go shopping downtown. Either she won't drive to the mountains or she won't go shopping, or maybe she'll do neither. Michelle thinks about when she started her new job. She knows that if she started a new job recently, then she got her paycheck this week. If the car has enough gas, did Michelle start a new job recently?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1074, "Jen wants to take a coastal drive and run errands if her car is in good shape. If her car is running smoothly, Jen can drive up the coast this weekend. If she changed the oil recently, she will also run errands around town. Either she can't take the drive or she can't run errands, or maybe neither. She tries to remember when her last mechanic appointment was. She knows that if her last mechanic appointment was 3 months ago, then she changed the oil recently. If Jen's car is running smoothly, was her last mechanic appointment 3 months ago?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1075, "Sara is waiting on a package of materials to complete a project she's working on. If the package was delivered on time, Sara will finish the project today. If the materials arrived undamaged, Sara will start planning her next project. Either Sara won't finish today or she won't plan the next project, or neither. Sara inspects the package and materials. She knows that if the driver handled them with care, then they arrived undamaged. If the package was delivered on time, did the driver handle it with care?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1076, "Lucy wants to make pancakes and cookies today. If the recipe calls for baking powder, she'll make pancakes for breakfast. If Lucy went grocery shopping yesterday, she'll also bake cookies this afternoon. Either she won't make pancakes or she won't bake cookies, or maybe she'll do neither. Lucy thinks back to when she got the recipes. She knows that if she downloaded new recipes last week, then she went grocery shopping yesterday. If the recipe calls for baking powder, did Lucy download new recipes last week?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1077, "John orders food online whenever he is busy with work. If John is busy with work, he opts for delivery. Getting food delivered saves time when John has a heavy workload. Either John did not order food online or he did not get delivery. Was John busy with work?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1078, "Whenever Kate feels stressed, she meditates. Kate also exercises when feeling anxious. Relaxation techniques and physical activity help manage stress. Either Kate did not meditate or she did not exercise. Was Kate feeling stressed?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1079, "If Jay notices the check engine light, he takes the car to the mechanic. Seeing the check engine light prompts Jay to check the owner's manual. Addressing warning lights right away prevents bigger issues down the road. Jay either did not go to the mechanic or he did not check the manual. Did Jay see the check engine light illuminated?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1080, "When Lisa goes camping, she packs extra blankets. If Lisa goes camping, she also brings warm clothes. Being prepared for cold nights is important when camping outdoors. Either Lisa did not pack extra blankets or she did not bring warm clothes. Did Lisa go camping?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1081, "Whenever Mark's computer runs slowly, he restarts it. Additionally, if Mark's computer is sluggish, he checks for any software updates. Keeping the computer updated improves performance over time. Mark either did not restart his computer or he did not check for updates. Is Mark's computer running slowly?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1082, "If Sam notices his car making unusual noises, he takes it to the mechanic. Also, if Sam hears strange car sounds, he inspects the engine. Addressing car problems promptly prevents further damage. Either Sam did not take his car to the mechanic, or he did not inspect the engine himself. Did Sam hear odd noises coming from his car?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1083, "When it's sunny outside, Lauren puts on sunscreen. Additionally, if it's a sunny day, Lauren wears a hat. Using sun protection prevents sunburn on bright days. Either Lauren did not apply sunscreen, or she did not wear a hat. Is it a sunny day outside?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1084, "Whenever it is sunny outside, Liam goes swimming. If the weather is sunny, Liam plays tennis. Sunny weather provides chances for Liam to enjoy outdoor activities. Either Liam did not go swimming or he did not play tennis. Was it sunny outside?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1085, "If the fire alarm goes off, Dan exits the building immediately. Additionally, if Dan hears the fire alarm, he alerts people nearby. Quickly evacuating and warning others is crucial for safety in case of a fire. Dan either did not exit the building, or he did not alert others. Did the fire alarm go off?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1086, "Whenever Mark notices a sale at the electronics store, he checks the prices. If there is a sale, Mark compares different models. Doing research during sales events helps get the best deals on new gadgets. Either Mark did not check the prices, or he did not compare models. Was there a sale at the electronics store?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1087, "If the stove is left on, the kitchen gets very warm. Also, if the stove is on, there is a burning smell in the house. This indicates the stove should be turned off when not in use. Either the kitchen is not warm or there is no burning smell. Was the stove left on?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1088, "If Sam notices the bag is heavy, he uses proper lifting techniques. Also, a heavy load prompts Sam to ask for help. Preventing injury is crucial when moving heavy objects. Either Sam did not use proper lifting techniques, or he did not ask for help. Was the bag Sam tried to lift heavy?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1089, "When Lisa goes hiking, she packs extra water. Lisa also brings a map if she goes hiking. Being prepared with supplies enables Lisa to hike safely. Either Lisa did not pack extra water or she did not bring a map. Did Lisa go hiking?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1090, "Whenever Mark has an exam coming up, he studies diligently. Also, if Mark has a test soon, he gets plenty of rest. Being well-prepared and well-rested helps Mark perform better academically. Either Mark did not study hard, or he did not get enough rest. Does Mark have an exam coming up soon?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1091, "Whenever Mark gets a flat tire, he changes it himself. Also, if Mark gets a flat, he calls roadside assistance. Being self-reliant and seeking help when needed are useful skills when dealing with car troubles. Either Mark did not change the tire himself, or he did not call for assistance. Did Mark get a flat tire?", ["Unknown.", "False."]],
  [1092, "It was a tough morning commute around the city. If it is rush hour, the traffic gets bad on the roads. If the traffic is bad, many people end up late for work. The trains also tend to have issues during rush hour. If the train is delayed, the passengers get frustrated. This morning, either it was rush hour, or the train was delayed, or both things occurred. If many people were not late for work, were the train passengers frustrated?", "True."],
  [1093, "Sara had a midterm exam in her hardest class today. If Sara studied many hours, she felt very prepared for the exam. If Sara felt prepared, she was likely to get an A. However, if the professor postponed the exam, then Sara would take it next week instead. Today, either Sara studied many hours, or the exam was postponed, or both happened. If Sara did not get an A on the exam, did she take it next week?", "True."],
  [1094, "It was a bad day for baking. If the ingredients are mixed improperly, the cake won't rise right while baking. If the cake doesn't rise properly, the cake tasting will be a disaster. Also if the oven is not working right, the cake will be undercooked. Today, either the ingredients were mixed improperly, or there was an issue with the oven, or both things occurred. If the cake tasting was not a disaster, was the cake undercooked?", "True."],
  [1095, "Last night we experienced some unusual weather. If the electricity goes out, the room becomes dark. If the room is dark, we light candles to see. If it starts raining, the streets get wet from the rain. Last night, either the electricity went out, it started raining, or both things happened. If we did not light any candles, did the streets get wet?", "True."],
  [1096, "Mary takes the bus to work each morning. If the bus is late, then Mary is late for work. If Mary is late for work, her boss gets upset. On the same route, if there is traffic on the highway, commuters get frustrated. This morning, either the bus was late, or there was highway traffic, or both occurred. If Mary's boss was not upset, were commuters frustrated?", "True."],
  [1097, "On a blustery day like today, strong winds can cause problems. If it is windy, tree branches can snap from the force. If branches snap, leaves end up scattered on the ground. Sam loves flying his kite, and windy days are perfect for it. If Sam flew his kite today, it went high in the sky. Either it was windy today, Sam flew his kite, or both things occurred. If there were no leaves scattered, did Sam's kite go high?", "True."],
  [1098, "The town was recovering from a major storm system that brought severe weather. If a tornado hit town, many buildings would become damaged. If buildings were damaged, debris would be everywhere. If a hurricane flooded the streets, cars would end up submerged. This storm system brought either a tornado, or flooding from a hurricane, or both. If there was no debris from damaged buildings, were cars submerged from flooding?", "True."],
  [1099, "ABC Company relies heavily on its sales performance. If the company has strong sales, then its revenue increases. If revenue increases, the company hires more employees. The company also recently opened a new factory. If the factory adds a new assembly line, then production increases there. This quarter, either sales were strong, or a new assembly line was added, or both things happened. If ABC Company did not hire more employees, did production increase at the factory?", "True."],
  [1100, "The farm was at the mercy of the weather this growing season. If the crops get enough sunlight, they will grow to maturity. With mature crops, there can be a successful harvest. However, if a drought hits, the crops will dry up while still in the fields. This year, either the crops got enough sunlight, or there was a drought, or both things happened. If the harvest was not successful, does that mean a drought destroyed the crops?", "True."],
  [1101, "It was a hectic morning in the Jones household. If the stove is left on, the pot boils over and makes a mess. If the pot boils over, there is a big mess to clean up. Also, if the dog gets into the trash, the floor ends up covered in garbage. Today, either the stove was left on, or the dog got into the trash, or both things happened. If there is no mess to clean up, is the floor covered in garbage?", "True."],
  [1102, "It was a tough week leading up to the product launch. If a deadline is unrealistic, employees have to cut corners to try meeting it. If corners are cut, the final product suffers. Also, if key staff are out sick, the timeline tends to slip. This past week, either the deadline was unrealistic, key people were out sick, or both things occurred. If the final product was not sloppy, did the project timeline slip?", "True."],
  [1103, "The local government had options for implementing policy changes. If the city council approved a proposal, an existing statute gets changed. If a statute is changed, then any new rules go into effect. Additionally, if voters reject a referendum, then no policy changes are made. This month, the city council either approved a proposal, or a referendum was rejected, or both occurred. If no new rules went into effect, does that no policy changes are made?", "True."],
  [1104, "It was an eventful concert last night. If the venue oversells tickets, it can dangerously exceed capacity. If the venue is over capacity, the fire marshal may get called to shut it down. Also, if a fight breaks out, the show will get cancelled for safety reasons. Last night, either the venue oversold tickets, there was a fight, or both things happened. If the fire marshal was not called, was the show cancelled?", "True."],
  [1105, "The software team had an important deadline coming up. If the deadline is approaching, the team ends up working overtime. If the team works overtime, they will complete the project on time. However, if the server crashes, they lose work and data. Either the deadline was approaching, or the server crashed, or both things occurred. If the project was not completed on time, did they lose work and data?", "True."],
  [1106, "It was an eventful Saturday in town. If it is the weekend, the mall gets very crowded as people have free time to shop. If the mall is crowded, there tend to be long lines at the registers. Also, yesterday was payday at many jobs. If it's payday, people have some extra money to spend. Today, either it was the weekend, or it was payday yesterday, or both things occurred. If there were no long lines, did people have money to spend?", "True."],
  [1107, "Nina wanted to become more fit. She knew that if she started a new workout routine, over time she would become stronger as her muscles developed. She realized that if the workout became easy, it would not be challenging enough anymore. Nina understood that if the workout was not challenging, she would have to increase the intensity to see continued progress. If Nina starts a new workout routine, does she increase the intensity?", "True."],
  [1108, "Jeff's alarm did not go off one morning, making him late to wake up. He knew that if he missed the bus, he would have to take a taxi instead. And if he had to take a taxi, his transportation costs for the month would go up. Jeff realized that if his transportation costs rose, it would put a strain on his monthly budget. If Jeff misses the bus to work, does his monthly budget feel strained?", "True."],
  [1109, "Jessica needs medication to manage her ongoing health condition. However, she recently was thinking of stopping taking her prescribed medication. She knows that if she stops taking it, her debilitating symptoms will return. And if her symptoms return, she will become unable to work at her job. Jessica understands that if she cannot work, her finances will take a hit. If Jessica stops taking her medication, do her finances suffer?", "True."],
  [1110, "Lucy had been feeling exhausted lately. She realized it may be because she wasn't getting enough sleep at night. Lucy knew that if she didn't get enough sleep, she would feel tired during the day. When she felt tired during the day, her productivity at work would decrease. She understood that if her productivity decreased, she would probably need to take a nap after work. If Lucy doesn't get enough sleep, does she take a nap after work?", "True."],
  [1111, "Emily had wanted a puppy for so long. She knew that if she got a puppy, she would have to play with it daily. By playing with the puppy daily, it would get well exercised. Emily was well aware that a well exercised puppy is usually a healthy puppy. If Emily gets a puppy, is the puppy healthy?", "True."],
  [1112, "Liz was dedicated to practicing her music every single day. She knew that if she practiced daily, she would improve her skills as a musician. After improving steadily, she got invited to audition for a local band. If she becomes quite skilled, she will earn a spot to join the band. She was excited that if she joined the band, they would start playing gigs all around town. If Liz practices music every day, does she start playing gigs around town?", "True."],
  [1113, "A city decided to build some new public parks in certain neighborhoods. The city knew that if it built nice new parks, more residents would start using them. With more people enjoying the parks, property values around them would increase. The city understood that if property values went up, it would end up generating higher tax revenue from those areas. If the city builds new parks, does it generate higher tax revenue?", "True."],
  [1114, "Mark decided he wanted to get in better shape. He knew that if he started eating a healthy diet, he would have more energy throughout the day. With this extra energy, he would feel motivated to exercise regularly. If Mark felt motivated to exercise regularly, he could lose weight over time. If Mark eats a healthy diet, does he lose weight?", "True."],
  [1115, "Sam had always dreamed of exploring outer space. He decided to study astronomy to learn more about the solar system. Sam knew that if he studied astronomy well, he would have a deep understanding of the the planets and stars. With strong knowledge of space, he could get accepted into NASA's space program. Sam realized that getting to work at NASA would allow him to live his dream. If Sam studies astronomy well, does he live his dream of space exploration?", "True."],
  [1116, "Mark owns a small business. He decided to invest in some new software to help manage operations. He knew that if he purchased the software, his team would need to learn how to use it properly. Mark realized that once his team learned the software, it would make them more productive. He understood that if their productivity increased, his business's profits would also likely improve. If Mark purchases new software, do profits improve?", "True."],
  [1117, "Amy was determined to become a better basketball player. She knew that if she practiced regularly, she would improve her skills. With improved skills, she would perform well during games. Amy realized that if she played well during games, her team would end up winning more matches. If Amy practices basketball regularly, does her team win more matches?", "True."],
  [1118, "Lily loves animals and started volunteering at the local animal shelter. She knew that if she volunteered, she would gain experience working with rescue dogs. After seeing how well Lily did, the shelter staff would ask her to foster dogs temporarily. From fostering, Lily would realize that she could provide a forever home for one of the dogs by adopting it herself. If Lily volunteers at the animal shelter, does she adopt one of her foster dogs?", "True."],
  [1119, "Looking to meet people, Ashley decided to try out a new hobby. She realized that if she put herself out there and tried something new, she would inevitably meet new people. As she got to know some of the people through her new hobby, Ashley ended up making a few close friends. She was happy that making new friends meant her overall social circle was growing larger. If Ashley tries a new hobby, does her social circle grow?", "True."],
  [1120, "It was monsoon season and the city could get heavy rainfall daily. The authorities knew that if the city gets heavy rainfall, the reservoirs would start filling up. And if the reservoirs kept filling up, then the risk of flooding would rise. The authorities had learned that if the risk of flooding rises, they need to issue flood warnings to the residents. If the city gets heavy rainfall, does the city issue flood warnings?", "True."],
  [1121, "James started a garden in his backyard. He learned that if he waters his plants daily, they will grow healthy and strong. When the plants are robust, they end up producing more flowers and vegetables. James understood that if his plants produced more yields, his garden would become plentiful. If James waters his plants daily, does he have a plentiful garden?", "True."],
  [1122, "Sarah always dreamed of becoming fluent in French and traveling to France. She learned that if she studied French every day, she would become fluent over time. Sarah knew fluency would allow her to comfortably travel to France someday. Whether it was studying, listening to French music, or both, Sarah immersed herself in the French language. If Sarah does not travel to France, then does she listen to French music?", "True."],
  [1123, "James has always wanted to travel the world and experience new cultures. He decided that if he took a foreign language class, he could start practicing speaking the language. With regular practice, James hoped to become fluent and comfortably conversant. Whether James is studying a new language or traveling internationally, he is expanding his cultural horizons. If James does not become fluent, then does he travel abroad?", "True."],
  [1124, "Emily wanted to maximize her productivity at work. She learned that if she got a good night's sleep consistently, she would feel well-rested and energized in the mornings. Feeling well-rested allowed Emily to stay focused during her workday. Whether it was prioritizing sleep, avoiding evening caffeine, or both, Emily took steps to optimize her sleep habits. If Emily does not stay focused at work, then does she avoid caffeine in the evenings?", "True."],
  [1125, "Jessica had a passion for musical theater but struggled with stage fright. She decided that if she took singing lessons, she would gain more confidence in her voice. And if she became more confident, she could finally audition for roles in musical theater productions in town. In her spare time, Jessica either took singing lessons, or wrote original songs, or did both to develop her musical talents. If Jessica does not audition for musical theater, then does she write songs?", "True."],
  [1126, "Dan wants to advance his career, so he makes an effort to network with professionals in his industry. He realizes that if he builds relationships, he'll start hearing about new job opportunities before they are publicly posted. And if he hears about them, he will get a step ahead of everyone. Whether Dan is networking to build connections, or working to improve his interview skills, he is taking steps forward in his career. If Dan does not get a step ahead of everyone, does he work on his interview skills?", "True."],
  [1127, "Ashley wanted to advance her career. She decided if she networks often, she'll meet industry professionals. Ashley knows meeting professionals means hearing about new job opportunities. Whether Ashley networks often, attends career fairs, or does both, she will make valuable connections. If Ashley does not hear about job opportunities, does she attend career fairs?", "True."],
  [1128, "Olivia set a goal to complete her first marathon this year. She knew that if she started training, she could slowly increase her endurance. The more her endurance improved, the more confident Olivia felt that she could go the distance and finish the marathon. Whether Olivia is diligently training or doing yoga each morning, she is strengthening her physical fitness to achieve her goal. If Olivia does not finish the marathon, then does she do yoga every morning?", "True."],
  [1129, "Chris decided to learn to code by practicing every day. He found that daily coding helped him build programming skills. Chris knew if he built up these skills, he could create complex web apps. Whether Chris codes daily, solves coding challenges to practice, or does both, his skills will grow. If Chris does not create web apps, does he solve coding challenges?", "True."],
  [1130, "Laura has dreamed of attending a prestigious music school. She learned that if she practices piano daily, her skills will steadily improve. Laura knows that gaining proficiency in piano could help her get accepted into the music program. While Laura spends hours each day on the piano, she also enjoys taking voice lessons during her free time. It's clear that Laura either devotes time to honing her piano skills, or focuses on developing her vocal talents, if not both. If Laura does not get accepted into music school, does she take voice lessons?", "True."],
  [1131, "Chris has a big exam coming up in his toughest class. He learns that if studies diligently, he'll have a strong grasp of the material. Chris knows that understanding the concepts could help him ace the test. In preparation, Chris spends late nights hitting the books. He also makes sure to get adequate sleep the night before the exam. Whether Chris studies hard or gets enough rest, or both, he wants to be ready to succeed. If Chris does not earn an A on the test, does he get enough sleep the night before?", "True."],
  [1132, "Emma wanted to make a difference for animals in need. She learned that if she volunteers at the local animal shelter, she can help care for the animals there. Emma knows that if the animals receive good care, they're more likely to get adopted into loving homes. In her free time, either Emma is volunteering with the animals, or donating much-needed supplies to the shelter, or doing both to help the cause. If the animals do not get adopted, does Emma donate supplies to the shelter?", "True."],
  [1133, "Chris wanted to become a web developer. He realized that if he learned web development, he would build valuable coding skills. And if he built these skills, Chris could start creating web apps from scratch. In his free time, Chris either learned web development, or played video games as a hobby, or did a bit of both when taking breaks from coding. If Chris does not create web apps, then does he play video games?", "True."],
  [1134, "Emma loves dogs and wants to adopt one of her own someday. She realized if she started volunteering at the local animal shelter, she could help dogs in need by supporting rescue efforts. The more Emma helped rescue dogs, the more attached she became to the idea of adopting one herself. Whether Emma volunteers with rescue dogs or donates to animal charities, she is dedicated to helping animals in need. If Emma does not adopt a dog, then does she donate to animal charities?", "True."],
  [1135, "Ryan has always loved music and dreamed of joining a band someday. He decided if he started taking guitar lessons, he could improve his guitar skills. Ryan knew that better skills would give him the confidence to audition for local bands. No matter what, Ryan is either taking guitar lessons to advance his skills, listening to music daily for inspiration, or doing both to immerse himself in the world of music. If Ryan does not audition for a band, then does he listen to music daily?", "True."],
  [1136, "Noah dreams of buying his own home someday. He learns that consistently saving each month will grow his savings funds. Noah knows he needs a healthy savings to afford a down payment. He also thinks of budgeting wisely to not overspend on unnecessary things. Whether saving or budgeting, Noah makes smart money choices. If Noah cannot afford a down payment, does he budget wisely?", "True."],
  [1137, "If a farmer waters their crops daily, the crops will grow healthy and strong. If there is a drought, then water restrictions will be put in place. Either the crops were watered daily, or there were no water restrictions, or the crops got watered but restrictions were not put in place. If crops are healthy and strong, then the harvest yield will be plentiful. There was a drought this season, does it mean the harvest yield plentiful on the farm?", "True."],
  [1138, "If the boss approves the budget, the project can move forward. If headquarters cuts funding, resources will be limited. Either the budget was approved, or resources are not limited, or the budget was approved and resources are not limited this quarter. It is known that if a project can move forward, the team will be highly productive. The headquarters cut funding this quarter, does this entail the project team highly productive?", "True."],
  [1139, "If the oven temperature is set properly, the cake will bake evenly. If it is someone's birthday, their family will throw a party for them. Either the oven was at the right temperature, or there was no birthday party, or the oven was at the proper heat but no party took place. When a cake is evenly baked all the way through, it tastes delicious. It was Jacob's birthday yesterday, can we say the cake taste delicious?", "True."],
  [1140, "If someone gets enough sleep, they will be well rested in the morning. If there is a snowstorm, then schools and businesses close for the day. Either Susan got enough rest, or schools did not close for the snowstorm, or Susan was well rested and yet schools stayed open during the storm. When people feel rested, their mood tends to improve throughout the day. There was a snowstorm last night, did Susan's mood improve today?", "True."],
